<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $23.1 mln April 25.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $23.1 mln April 25.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $23.1 million surplus on April 25 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON APRIL 25</p>
<p>Exports: $232.8 million</p>
<p>Imports: $231.7 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $309.7 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $287.7 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $23.1 million</p>
<p>ARPIL DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $4.080 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $4.266 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $5.297 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $4.327 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $784 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
